<section class="shell band faq">
  <h2>Questions about depression therapy</h2>

  <details>
    <summary>What if I feel nothing rather than sad?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Numbness is one of the more common presentations here and it is worth taking as
      seriously as sadness. It usually means a system turned the volume down on everything to
      survive something, and the work is restoring range rather than chasing a mood.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Is this depression or burnout?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>The distinction matters less than what maintains it. Both tend to involve a nervous
      system that has been running on override for a long time. What we look at is what the
      shutdown is protecting and what would have to be true for it to relax.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do you work with procrastination?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>Yes, and specifically the kind that has outlasted every system you have tried. The
      working assumption is that a part of you is holding the brake for a reason worth knowing,
      rather than that you need better discipline.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>Do I need antidepressants?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>That is a question for a prescriber. Reem is a Licensed Professional Counselor
      Supervisor, not a physician, and does not prescribe or advise on medication. Therapy and
      medication are not alternatives to each other, and plenty of people do both.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>I have been in therapy before and it did not help. Why would this be different?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>It might not be, and that is worth saying in the consult. What is different here is
      the lens: body-based and developmental rather than insight-led, on the view that
      understanding your history and changing nothing is a common and frustrating place to get
      stuck.</p>
    </div>
  </details>

  <details>
    <summary>What if I am thinking about ending my life?</summary>
    <div class="answer-body">
      <p>This practice does not provide emergency or crisis care. Call or text 988 for the
      Suicide and Crisis Lifeline, or 911 if you are in immediate danger. Once you are safe,
      a consult here can be a next step rather than the first one.</p>
    </div>
  </details>
